26 1 26 ...</span><br> $ legend.t  : chr  &quot;Communities (#)&quot; &quot;Communities (#)&quot; &quot;Communities (#)&quot; &quot;Communities (#)&quot; ...<br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"> $ color     : Factor w/ <b>22 levels</b> &quot;red&quot;,&quot;green&quot;,..: 1 1 1 1 1 1 22 22 1 22 ...</span><br> $ color.text: chr  &quot;red&quot; &quot;red&quot; &quot;red&quot; &quot;red&quot; ...<br> - attr(*, &quot;.internal.selfref&quot;)=&lt;externalptr&gt; <br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>As you can see, I&#39;ve highlighted in blue the rows of memb and color for both data.table. I don&#39;t know how to make it have the same number of memb and color. Also, I don&#39;t know if this error is due to having a brain segmentation too small and there are too many comunities.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Regards,</div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
